   "author": "Hollowmere team (agent X)",
   "story": "Camp Tamarack was a church summer camp on the lake: four cabins round the flagpole and the fire ring, a mess hall, the staff lodge, an infirmary cabin and a canoe shed, and Ruth Halvorsen, who had directed it for twenty-two summers. When the Cordon closed the roads it made the camp Family Evacuation Point 6. Thirty-one families came with what they could carry; the Cordon registered them on a board under the gate, one family a cabin and the rest on mats in the mess hall, and on the third morning the buses took every child under fourteen. The second convoy, for the parents, was coming Thursday. Ruth called Convoy Control on the lodge radio at nine every night and heard static. The fever came with a late family. Nell, the camp nurse, filled the infirmary; Ruth padlocked the sick cabins at night and kept the walk-in full of the convoy's stores, untouched, for when it came. When her own hands went cold she sat down in the walk-in with the stores and had Corporal Ames lock it behind her, the key on her board in the office. Ames took a canoe across the lake to find a phone. The families are still at the long tables, waiting for their turn.",
